title: The Psalms of David's Flight, Part 3 – The Hunted King
description: The Psalms of David's Flight, Part 3 of 3: the Ziphites betray David (Psalm 54, 1 Samuel 23), and David prays in the cave and spares Saul (Psalm 57, 1 Samuel 24), the two Psalm studies read in full, in the King James Bible.
output: lessons/bible/davids-flight-3-the-hunted-king.html

# The Psalms of David's Flight, part 3 of 3 (a Wednesday-night lesson, read aloud from a laptop, about 30-35 minutes).
# Layout: as in the note at the top of davids-flight-1-the-flight-begins.deck; after "Where we are" a "Previously"
# slide names the passages of Parts 1 and 2.
# Built from, in full and in their own order:
#   Psalm 54 study (review/refile.json drive "psalms-54"; Psalms.json -> studies -> "54")
#   Psalm 57 study, both parts: the prayer in the cave, then 1 Samuel 24 (drive "psalms-57"; Psalms.json -> "57")
# Verses the studies typed out are shown from the KJV by the builder. Words of the psalm that sit inside a sentence
# of the study (Save me, Hear my prayer, Behold, God is my helper) stay in the sentence as typed.
# Fixed: "the love the one" -> "the love of the one" was already fixed in the app's text; "during this time especially
# this incident" -> "during this time, especially this incident". Nothing else.

